      "body": "\n## Motivation\n\nCRIU restore can reset process CPU time below the monitor’s saved baseline. The resulting negative delta causes the Prometheus counter to raise ValueError, terminating the monitoring thread and leaving CPU metrics stale.\n\n## Modifications\n\nCount the current CPU reading as time since restore when the delta is negative, then update the baseline for subsequent samples.\n\nAdd a regression using a real Prometheus counter covering repeated resets and normal increments after each reset.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nModel outputs are unaffected.\n\nBoth mocked CPU-monitor tests pass directly without GPU dependencies or stubs. The new regression reproduces the negative-counter failure against the original implementation.\n\nFull-file execution encounters existing interference from the smoke test’s background thread. Real CRIU restore validation remains outstanding.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable. This change affects background CPU telemetry and does not modify inference execution.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Applicable pre-commit checks pass.\n- [x] Add focused regression coverage.\n- [x] Follow existing CPU-monitor test structure and formatting.\n- Documentation: not applicable; no user-facing interface changes.\n- Accuracy and speed benchmarks: not applicable.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38746066287](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38746066287)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38746066317](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38746066317)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38746066175](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38746066175)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
